      "rev_n_2_90100d_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_90100d_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_90100d",
        "thought_text": "I understand the issue. The current approach doesn't correctly handle cases where the sum of the first half equals the sum of the second half. Instead, we need to ensure that the sum of the first half is equal to the sum of the second half plus the last odd number in the second half. This adjustment will correctly solve the problem for all test cases.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_90100d_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_f8d69a23a3",
        "created_at": 1794528172.4470768
      },
      "rev_n_1_057eaa_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_057eaa_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_057eaa",
        "thought_text": "The previous approach correctly identifies that n must be divisible by 4 for a solution to exist. However, it doesn't account for the possibility of overflow when constructing the array. For very large n, the even numbers in the first half could exceed 10^9, violating the constraint that all elements must be positive and not exceed 10^9.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_057eaa_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_2f8ee2e3c2",
        "created_at": 1794528203.1032467
      },
      "rev_n_3_04c3e8_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_04c3e8_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_04c3e8",
        "thought_text": "Ensure the sums of both sequences are equal by carefully selecting even and odd numbers to balance the sums while maintaining distinctness and positivity.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_04c3e8_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_c1dff277e8",
